-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",393,{
[12545]="7006AFD2\n1\tDefeat Deshûkh smugglers (total: 8)\tYou should investigate Deshûkh for signs of Amârbo. Deshûkh is located north-west of the Dûlkar.\n2\tSearch for Amârbo in Deshûkh\tSearch for Amârbo in Deshûkh, the Blood Market.\n3\tAsk Amârbo what he knows of Sêkhta and his whereabouts\tAsk Amârbo what he knows of Sêkhta and his whereabouts.\n4\tReturn to Khôltekh in Dâr Laja with this information\tReturn to Khôltekh in Dâr Laja, Hall of the Kindred, with this information.\n",
[12546]="7006AFDF\n1\tFind Dar Sêkhta in Dil-irmíz\tKhôltekh has asked you to look for Dar Sêkhta, and a suspicious lock there that might fit a mysterious key. According to Amârbo, it is located south of Deshûkh in Dil-irmíz.\n2\tLook for a door within Dar Sêkhta with a suspicious lock\tLook for an alcove or door with an unconventional lock.\n3\tExamine the strange lock for clues as to its key\tExamine the strange lock for clues as to its key.\n4\tReturn to Dâr Laja and tell Khôltekh your description of the lock\tReturn to Dâr Laja with your description of the lock. Perhaps Khôltekh has a clue as to its key.\n5\tSpeak with Khôltekh when you are ready to go\tAccompany Khôltekh to his house, so he may think clearly on this key.\n",
[12547]="7006B07C\n1\tFind a pristine crypt-walker's hand by defeating crypt-walkers\tKhôltekh has asked you to go to Sektakhâb in Khabârkhad and find a pristine wight's hand. He believes this is the key to Dâr Sêkhta that will open the way and find Sêkhta or necessary clues about him.\n2\tFind a pristine crypt-walker's hand by defeating crypt-walkers\tKhôltekh has asked you to go to Sektakhâb in Khabârkhad and find a pristine wight's hand. He believes this is the key to Dâr Sêkhta that will open the way and find Sêkhta or necessary clues about him.\n3\tGo back to Dâr Sêkhta and insert the pristine wight's hand into the lock\tGo back to Dâr Sêkhta and insert the pristine wight's hand into the lock.\n4\tEnter the hidden area of Dâr Sêkhta\tEnter the hidden area of Dâr Sêkhta.\n5\tReturn to Khôltekh in Dâr Laja with the clues you have found\tReturn to Khôltekh in Dâr Laja with the clues you have found.\n",
[12548]="7006B07B\n1\tSpeak with Ephrâti in Tilmakhím in Tâkhdar\tFind a bookseller named Ephrâti in Tilmakhím, in Tâkhdar. Khôltekh is looking for the missing volume from the set you found in Dâr Sêkhta.\n2\tReturn to Khôltekh in Dâr Laja with the book\tReturn to Khôltekh in Dâr Laja with the book.\n3\tSpeak with Khôltekh when you are ready to go\tAccompany Khôltekh to the Tor-gardens.\n4\tSpeak with Khôltekh about his revelation\tSpeak with Khôltekh outside the Pot and Quill in the Tor-gardens about his revelation.\n",
[12549]="7006B07D\n1\tSpeak with Khôltekh when you are ready to go\tSpeak with Khôltekh to go to the Sail-haven.\n2\tSpeak with Khôltekh in Dâr Laja\tSpeak with Khôltekh in Dâr Laja.\n",
[12550]="70001731\n1\tTalk to Garvan\tGarvan is in the city of Donnvail, north-east of Fail-á-Khro. Búdan told you of the three leaders sent to Donnvail by Carn Dûm: Fûshath the Beast, Muiráthakh the Silent Judge, and Gillë Andras the Lord of the Western Marches. He also told you to speak to a Man named Garvan further within the city of Donnvail.\n2\tTalk to Morven\tMorven is within the city of Donnvail, north-east of Fail-á-Khro. Garvan gave you the name of someone who might be sympathetic to the cause, telling you to seek Morven further into the city.\n3\tTalk to Uthagan\tUthagan is in the city of Donnvail, north-east of Fail-á-Khro. Morven has told you to speak with Uthagan, but with caution: his family was recently taken by Muiráthakh, and she does not think they have been seen since.\n4\tTalk to Una\tUthagan spoke of Una, located somewhere within the city of Donnvail, north-east of Fail-á-Khro. Though he sought to slay you, Uthagan unwittingly gave you the name of someone you might speak to: a woman named Una.\n",
[12551]="7002C609\n1\tTalk to Captain Agelbrit\tSpeak with Captain Agelbrit at the Limlight Gorge Guard-house.\n2\tTalk to Sigelm\tSigelm is near the Limlight Gorge Guardhouse. Captain Agelbrit has asked you to listen to Sigelm's tales of the Limlight Gorge before you explore the dangerous valley.\n3\tTalk to Captain Agelbrit\t\n",
[12552]="7002C5F5\n1\tTalk to Armund in the old sawmill\tYou should find the old sawmill in the Limlight Gorge and learn if Armund and his companions are still alive.\n",
[12553]="700682D8\n1\tTalk to Adranax at the agreed upon location\tJavish has asked you to initiate negotiations between a renegade Corsair group which poses a threat to the status quo in Mâr Naphra. The meeting location should be among the shallows to the south-east.\n2\tTalk to Javish\tAdranax planned to betray Javish all along. Javish should know that you had no choice but to defend yourself. Javish can be found in Mâr Naphra.\n3\tDefeat Corsairs in Khataj Mârsa (total: 8)\tJavish has no choice but to take Adranax's actions as an act of sedition. He asks that we punish the Corsairs before they can cause further chaos. Khataj Mârsa can be found south-east of Mâr Naphra.\n4\tTalk to Javish in Mâr Naphra\tThe Corsairs at Khataj Mârsa have been punished. You should report to Javish your success. Javish can be found in Mâr Naphra.\n",
[12554]="70067537\n1\tReturn the bandanas to Tagar in Jax Phanâl\030Collect goblin bandanas from Súlstrok or environs ([see journal]/12)\tTagar asked that you return to the goblins' encampment south and east of Jax Phanâl in a further attempt to remove the goblin threat from the area. You are to collect twelve of the goblins' bandanas, and return them to Tagar at his dwelling.\n",
[12555]="7002BFF8\n1\tDefeat Sherkóz\tThe trainer of the Khundolar battle-cats may be found at Lashkarg, south-east of Etheburg in the Brown Lands. Twiga asked you to hunt down the trainer of the Khundolar battle-cats and defeat him.\n2\tTalk to Twiga at Etheburg in the Brown Lands\tTwiga is at Etheburg in the Brown Lands, north-west of Lashkarg. You should return to Twiga with tidings of your victory.\n",
[12556]="70067F93\n1\tGather insects (total: 5)\tRaghda-gûn asked you to gather insects to feed to her little adoptee. Insects can be found underneath little stones scattered around the Raghda-gûn's nest.\n2\tTalk to Raghda-gûn\tYou have gathered enough insects to feed little Berkha. Return to Raghda-gûn.\n",
[12557]="700529E3\n1\tFind the Elf at the Beorning watchpost\tAn Elf was sent to the Beorning Watchpost in Gladden Fields by the Woodfolk in Laerlad. You should see if this Elf made it to the watchpost.\n2\tTalk to Baradal\tYou have found the Elf at the Beorning watchpost on the edge of the Gladden Fields. You should talk to the Elf.\n",
[12558]="7003A662\n1\tCollect skipping stones (total: 4)\tThe falls of Everholt lie to the south-west of Beaconwatch. Lady Answith wants to go to the falls in Everholt and collect several stones that would be suitable for skipping.\n2\tTalk to Lady Answith\tLady Answith is on a porch above the vendor's area north of the Mead Hall in Beaconwatch. You have collected skipping stones at the Everholt Falls and should now bring them back to Lady Answith.\n",
[12559]="700309E7\n1\tBring powder-kegs to the central pit of the Living Deep (quantity: see journal)\tPowder-kegs can be found within the Living Deep. Dernstan asked you to venture within the Living Deep and safely destroy the enemy's black powder.\n2\tTalk to Dernstan\tDernstan is at Eaworth. Dernstan will be pleased to hear you have safely destroyed several barrels of black powder.\n",
[12560]="7002F308\n1\tDefeat goblins in the Living Deep (total: 10)\tGoblins can be found in the Living Deep.\n2\tTalk to Dernstan\tDernstan is at Eaworth. Dernstan will be pleased to hear you defeated several goblins within the Living Deep.\n",
[12561]="700164E1\n1\tDefeat deep-toads (total: 8)\tDeep-toads can be found all over the Water-works. Águti believes that when the toads are killed, the lizards and spiders will fall upon each other for food.\n2\tTalk to Águti in the Rotting Cellar\tÁguti is in the Rotting Cellar. Águti will be pleased to hear the deep-toad population has been thinned.\n",
[12562]="700078EB\n1\tTalk to Mason Thorne at the Combe lumber-camp\tMason Thorne is at the lumber-camp, north and east of the guard-house. Ted Pickthorn asked you to speak with Mason Thorne, the foreman at the Combe lumber-camp. He may recall which tree had been the Hanging Tree.\n2\tBring the ledger to Mason Thorne\030Collect Mason Thorne's ledger\tMason Thorne awaits you at the lumber-camp that lies east and north of Combe, south of the Chetwood. Thorne sent you to retrieve his ledger from the Blackwold brigands encamped along the road. You should return the ledger to him at once.\n",
[12563]="7004327D\n1\tSearch the Crossings of Erui for sign of the Lone Lady\tThe Crossings of Erui can be found far to the north of Halach in eastern Upper Lebennin. Glassiel has asked you to search the Crossings of Erui for any sign of the mysterious Lone Lady.\n2\tDisturb the nearby pile of river-stones\tRiver-stones can be found at the Crossings of Erui in eastern Upper Lebennin. You have found only a drowned Haradrim and should now search for the Lone Lady of Erui.\n3\tAttempt to talk to the Lone Lady\tThe Lone Lady can be found at the Crossings of Erui in eastern Upper Lebennin. After disturbing a pile of river-stones, the Lone Lady has appeared in a rage. You should attempt to speak to her.\n4\tTalk to Glassiel\tGlassiel can be found in Halach in south-eastern Upper Lebennin. The Lone Lady has given her waters form using pieces of ancient armour and has banished you from the Erui. You should bring these dire tidings to Glassiel.\n",
[12564]="70065656\n1\tTalk to Handir\tYou have found a lonely dog in East Pelargir. A nearby guard, Handir, has called out to you.\n2\tTalk to Handir\tYou have found a lonely dog in East Pelargir. A nearby guard, Handir, has called out to you.\n3\tFeed the lonely dog\tHandir has given you some meat with which to feed the lonely dog.\n4\tTalk to Handir\tYou have fed the lonely dog. You should talk to Handir.\n",
[12565]="7004A397\n1\tSearch the northward road\tYou should follow the road that winds north from western Udûn.\n2\tContinue up the road\tYou should continue up the road that winds north from western Udûn.\n3\tRaise the Gondorian banner\tYou should raise the fallen Gondorian banner that you found on the road that winds north from western Udûn.\n4\tYou should continue up the road that winds north from western Udûn, righting any other banners that you find.\t\n5\tContinue up the road, fixing any other fallen banners you find\tYou should continue up the road that winds north from western Udûn.\n6\tTalk to the look-out\tYou should talk to the look-out on the outcropping off the road that winds north from western Udûn, and learn what he knows of Captain Lachír.\n7\tLook next to Coldan\tThe soldier Coldan has asked you to stand beside him and look up toward the looming face of Ered Lithui.\n8\tTalk to Coldan\tColdan the look-out stands on the outcropping off the road that winds north from western Udûn. You should talk to Coldan again, now that you looked and have seen the great edifice against the mountains.\n",
[12566]="70060D88\n1\tCollect the Yonder-watch supplies from the secret store-hole\tYonder-watch supplies can be found at the secret store-hole in the woods between Gamwich and Long Cleeve. You should carry Yonder-watch supplies to a Bounder in Long Cleeve. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tTalk to Bounder Tudge in Long Cleeve\tA Bounder of the Yonder-watch can be found in Long Cleeve. You should talk to Bounder Tudge in Long Cleeve.\n3\tConfront Bill Ferny\tBill Ferny can be found near Long Cleeve in the Yondershire. You should confront Bill Ferny.\n4\tTalk to Fredegar Bolger at the secret store-hole\tA secret Yonder-watch store-hole can be found in the woods between Gamwich and Long Cleeve. You should talk to Fredegar Bolger at the store-hole.\n",
[12567]="70058CFA\n1\tDestroy Orkish trebuchets at Hanksar-mokh and Kulûg-mokh (total: 6)\030Destroy Orkish ballistae at Hanksar-mokh and Kulûg-mokh (total: 4)\tOrkish trebuchets and ballistae can be found in Hanksar-mokh and Kulûg-mokh. Darfin has asked you to destroy the siege-engines deployed in Hanksar-mokh and Kulûg-mokh. You should destroy Orkish trebuchets and ballistae.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have destroyed many Orkish trebuchets and ballistae at Hanksar-mokh and Kulûg-mokh.\n",
[12568]="7003A695\n1\tCross the bridge to leave Gapholt\tThe time has come to leave Gapholt and return to Woodhurst. You will need to pass over the bridge to begin your return journey.\n2\tWestan calls for your attention\tWestan is on the bridge leading into Gapholt. Westan saw you coming and called for your attention.\n3\tTravel to Mate Isernore\tMate Isernore is along the road between Gapholt and Woodhurst. Mate Isernore was once a mine owned by Gifemund, but was taken by the White Hand who crossed the Swiftwater River.\n4\tMate Isernore is along the road between Gapholt and Woodhurst. White Hand scourge should be wiped out of Mate Isernore and out of the northern Stonedeans. The mine and its resources were not theirs to take.\t\n5\tTalk to Herubrand\tHerubrand is in the cellar of the farmhouse in Woodhurst. You should return to Herubrand to inform him of your success in bringing aid from Gapholt and defeating the White Hand forces in Mate Isernore.\n",
[12569]="70053F48\n1\tStoke the fires (total: 6)\tFire pits can be found at Adambel. You should stoke the fires.\n2\tSoldiers can be found at Adambel. You should talk with the soldiers to pass the time.\t\n3\tTalk to Habhûk\tHabhûk can be found at Adambel. You should talk to Habhûk.\n",
[12570]="7000E4DF\n1\tDefeat kalpa-kita (total: 12)\030Defeat Pitkä-hammas\tKalpa-kita can be found at Leijona-kotin, east of Jänis-leiri. Niko wants you to cull the numbers of kalpa-kita in the area and especially to defeat a vicious cat named Pitkä-hammas.\n2\tTalk to Niko\tNiko is at Jänis-leiri, west from Leijona-kotin. You should return to Niko and tell him of your success.\n",
[12571]="7006AA08\n1\tTalk to Porókho\tPorókho would like to speak with you privately. Porókho is in Hêbatokh, the clan Morutágya camp in Ilmabiri, beneath the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl.\n2\tTalk to Belondor in Dâr Laja\tAfter helping the grateful Morutágya clan with their requests, you feel that you have been dismissed. You should return to Belondor in Dâr Laja, the Meeting Hall and tell him what you learned.\n",
[12572]="7005A801\n1\tTalk to Dáin\tDáin can be found at Durin's Stone. After overcoming Azog's forces at Durin's Stone, Náin Orcsfoe and the Iron-folk prepare to again make for the gates of Moria. You should talk to Dáin.\n2\tTalk to Dáin at Muru Azog\tDáin can be found just outside Muru Azog at Azanulbizar. Azog has been slain at last, but victory was won at great cost. You should talk to Dáin.\n3\tTalk to King Thráin at Muru Azog\tKing Thráin can be found just outside Muru Azog at Azanulbizar. Azog has been slain at last, but Dáin has fallen silent. You should talk to King Thráin.\n",
[12573]="700436CF\n1\tDefeat Easterlings in the Brotherhood of the Pinioned (total: 5)\tFollowers of the Brotherhood of the Pinioned can be found throughout Osgiliath, and often wander far from their Easterling brethren. You recall Echil's mentioning of a \"Lord of Pinions\" among the Easterlings who now form a brotherhood under him. You should seek out and defeat his followers to learn more of his whereabouts. NOTE: You must defeat all five groups of Easterling followers to unlock the optional Lord of Pinions encounter.\n2\tDefeat the Lord of Pinions\tThe Lord of Pinions can be found in the north-eastern corner of Osgiliath. You have weakened the Brotherhood of the Pinioned, and should now confront the Lord of Pinions in Osgiliath.\n",
[12574]="70015E0F\n1\tThe Uruk Gâmzhurm can be found south and slightly west of Echad Dúnann, across Nan Sirannon. You must use the horn of challenge to summon Gâmzhurm, the leader of the Dunlendings, and defeat him.\t\n2\tTalk to Glavroleth at Echad Dúnann\tGlavroleth is at Echad Dúnann, north and slightly east of Porth Cadlus. You should return to Glavroleth with the news of Gâmzhurm's death.\n",
[12575]="700083A6\n1\tDefeat Gillë Andras\tGillë Andras, the Lord of the Western Marches, can be found within the city of Dûn Covád, in the western foothills north of Fail-á-Khro. Soltakh has asked you and your allies to defeat Gillë Andras, the Lord of the Western Marches.\n2\tTalk to Soltakh\tSoltakh is at Fail-á-Khro, north of Aughaire and south of Dûn Covád. You have defeated Gillë Andras, the Lord of the Western Marches, and should now bring news of your triumph to Soltakh.\n",
[12576]="70066612\n1\tTalk to Malthellam in Morlad\tMalthellam can be found outside his home in Morlad in the Blackroot Vale. You have been told to travel to Morlad to seek an audience with the Steward of the Vale, Malthellam, and gain the Lord's permission to remain in the Blackroot Vale.\n",
})
